{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "02-review-chain",
  "title": "Pre-PR review pack on Archon",
  "description": "Pre-PR review as an Archon workflow pack, from trigger to outside reviewers.\n\n- **Trigger** (top-left): GitHub pull_request binding (pr.lifecycle) passes a receipt to Resource admission (capacity 1, overlap queue), which admits one run into scope (wire enters scope from the left, clear of the rounds header).\n- **Review pack** (`.archon/workflows/codecaine/review/`) holds the **rounds** loop_group (max_iterations 5), drawn as a U on a 4-column grid: top row scope → mode → pack-context → route; bottom row returns review-complete → extract-findings → synthesize → publish; publish → ready? (left column) loops up to scope (not ready) or exits to tag-outside-reviewers (ready, dashed).\n- Between the rows: the **archon-review-block** lenses (3+2) sit right, under route and above review-complete; the **Coding-agent reviewers** (Codex, Claude) sit left. route fans out on two trunks: the upper one (\"starts both\") enters each reviewer from the right, the lower one (\"picks lenses\") drops into each lens. Every lens and reviewer wires into review-complete along one fan-in trunk (\"all_done\" on the reviewer side).\n- **Proposed tail** (dashed): tag-outside-reviewers tags Greptile and CodeRabbit in Outside reviewers (bottom-left).\n- **Stores** (bottom-middle): a trace.db subsection holds one container per kernel node; teal kernel-span wires drop from pack-context (via the corridor between reviewers and lenses) and extract-findings (straight). workflow_events gets one wire from the whole pack frame.\n- Color key: violet model node, teal kernel node, blue script/bash node, green lens, orange gate/check, yellow store; dashed = proposed.",
  "mode": "diagram",
  "viewport": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "zoom": 1
  },
